From: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: optimize cgroup_threadgroup_rwsem fast-path for dynamic thread creation

Fast-path percpu_down_read_trylock in cgroup_threadgroup_change_begin to favor
uncontended dynamic thread creation. Leaves cgroup struct layouts untouched
for full GKI 6.1 KMI preservation.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
---
 kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
@@ -2965,6 +2965,10 @@ void cgroup_threadgroup_change_begin(struct task_struct *tsk)
 {
 	might_sleep();
 
+	/* Fast-path dynamic thread creation without waiting */
+	if (likely(percpu_down_read_trylock(&cgroup_threadgroup_rwsem)))
+		return;
+
 	percpu_down_read(&cgroup_threadgroup_rwsem);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(cgroup_threadgroup_change_begin);
-- 
2.43.0
